    "explanation": "Both of you agree on where the car went; the dispute is what that trip should have cost. Trip TRP-00514's GPS trace records 11.75 km of driving against a booked optimal route of 5.1 km — an excess of 6.65 km, or 130.4% of the optimal distance. The trace figure governs over the trip record's rounded 11.8 km (POL-RD-01). That clears both establishment tests (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km), so the deviation is established, and since it also exceeds 50% it is a material deviation.\n\nNothing excuses it. POL-RD-03 requires a traffic advisory naming a road the optimal route uses; EV-ADVIS-00514-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT — no advisory covers this corridor), so there is no advisory to read and the driver's 'the direct road was heavy' explanation is a bare assertion that POL-RD-08 says does not discharge the burden. The chat log EV-CHAT-00514 is empty, so there is no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04. No endpoint was amended, so POL-RD-05 does not apply. The vehicle was RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The fare is METERED with no quoted fare, so POL-RD-02 governs rather than POL-RD-11.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic, not discretionary. Charged total was SGD 19.61. The recomputed fare is ((SGD 3.80 base + 0.75 × 5.1 km = SGD 3.825 + 0.28 × 9.0 min = SGD 2.52) × the 1.0 surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + SGD 0.80 platform fee = SGD 10.945. The difference is SGD 19.61 − 10.945 = SGD 8.665, rounded up to SGD 8.70. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, and at 44.2% of the charge it is well below the 90% share that would make it a full refund. Rider, you are refunded SGD 8.70 and the balance of SGD 10.91 stands. Your demand for the whole SGD 19.61 is not supported by the fare arithmetic.\n\nNo pass-through correction is added: the fare breakdown's ERP total is SGD 0.00, there are no tolls and no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing in either direction and the SGD 8.70 is the driver's total liability here. The driver's profile shows no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 across completed_trips_90d 250, ratio 0.00, below POL-RD-06's 0.05 with its 40-trip floor), so no POL-RD-06(b) uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral; the profile counters were used only for the test POL-RD-06 names. The trace is clean for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — 100% coverage, 133 fixes at the expected 10 s interval, no gaps — so no independent corroboration is required and the finding rests on it and the trip record, both at full weight. No clause produces a referral on these facts. The rider's point that the trip was run by a partner fleet is noted, but it is a service complaint, not a billing-integrity or conduct finding on this record, and it does not change the money."
