    "explanation": "To both parties: the fare on this trip was metered (fare_breakdown EV-FARE-00514 records fare_model METERED and quoted_fare_sgd null), so POL-RD-11 does not bite and POL-RD-02 governs the remedy. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00514, weight 1.0, 133 fixes at a 10 s interval, coverage 100%, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0) measures 11.75 km of driving against a booked optimal of 5.1 km — an excess of 6.65 km, or 130.39% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment limbs pass (over 20% and over 0.8 km), and because the excess also exceeds 50% it is additionally a MATERIAL deviation, which required the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across completed_trips_90d of 250, so no repeat pattern is established, no POL-RD-06(b) uplift applies and no conduct referral is made. The driver's explanation that 'traffic on the direct road was heavy' is not supported by any advisory. EV-ADVIS-00514-01 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT: no advisory covers the optimal corridor in this window), so POL-RD-03 cannot run — no advisory names a road the optimal route uses and there is no validity window to match. Under POL-RD-08 a general assertion that traffic was bad, citing no traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the driver's burden, so that assertion carries no weight. His counterparty statement's admission that he 'went around' is consistent with the trace but adds nothing, since the trace alone decides the excess. No other clause excuses the excess: EV-CHAT-00514 has zero messages, so there was no rider-requested detour (POL-RD-04) and no address change (POL-RD-05); pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null; the vehicle was RYDE_X, not a pool, so POL-RD-12 does not apply and solo_optimal_distance_km is irrelevant; and the trace is clean for policy purposes under POL-RD-07, so the deviation stands on the trace alone. The refund is arithmetic: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 × 5.1 km + 0.28 × 9.0 min) × 1.0 surge multiplier (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 10.945. Refund = charged_total 19.61 − 10.945 = 8.665, rounded up to SGD 8.70. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and 44.2% of charged_total, well short of the 90% share that would convert the outcome to FULL_REFUND, so the balance of the charge stands. Nothing is added on top: the fare breakdown's ERP total is 0.00, tolls_erp is 0.0 and there is no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09 gives no separate pass-through correction, and no line is billed short of the trace, so no POL-RD-04 driver compensation arises. The rider's request for the whole SGD 19.61 is not supported, because the recomputed optimal trip leaves the base, distance and time charges payable; the driver's position that his liability is bounded by the POL-RD-02 figure is correct. The rider's point that the trip was fulfilled by a partner fleet is noted but is not a ground any clause attaches a remedy to. No escalation trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired, trip IDs and timestamps match across all artifacts, no charge line lacks a counterpart, the refund is far below SGD 150.00, confidence is above the floor, and the driver's traffic assertion is a discarded assertion under POL-RD-08 rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a missing artifact.",
